==Battleground==
*1 [[Johnnyleon]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Zamelle]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Razorback]] spawns after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Dread Bore]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The actually threatening enemies take a while to spawn, so use that time to stack [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-control units]] and/or [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attackers]] to deal with the Bores and the Angelic Sleipnir respectively. Try not to spawn too many meatshields during this phase so as to conserve money. The use of [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|cats with the Knockback ability]] is also discouraged due to the risk of pushing into Zamelle's range.

[[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] is very useful to stall [[Zamelle]] and [[Dread Bore]] without using too much money. [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] can also be used against the Sleipnir for similar reasons.

The [[Holy Blast|Holy Blast Cannon]] can be used to prevent Dread Bore from burrowing.

If one wishes to finish the stage quickly, it's possible to use Razorback's money drop to send out attackers and kill the remaining enemies before the Dread Bore even spawns.

==Trivia==
*Border Between Worlds refers to the border between the world of the living and the world after death, hence the [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]]; its Japanese name can be literally translated as "Border Between This World and That World", but あの世 ''ano yo'' ("that world") is a euphemism for the world after death.

